# Coding Task: Phase 5A — Flexible Inputs, Enhanced Patch Stems, THOR Integration

## Context
Read `CLAUDE.md`, `results.md`, `science.md` before starting. This is Phase 5 of the `exp-7-clean-slate` branch. The baseline (`7A_geocv_baseline`) is done. This phase makes three additive changes to prepare for ablation studies:

1. **Enhanced `PatchTokenStem`** with LayerNorm + 2-layer MLP (instead of bare linear projection). Motivated by the observation that per-modality normalisation before fusion (same principle that made TESSERA work in 7A) should also help THOR + TerraMind patch tokens, which come from different SSL objectives and have mismatched embedding statistics.

2. **THOR patch token support** wired into `DualEncDualDecFusion` via the same sensor-routed skip injection already used for TerraMind. S1-type → height decoder. S2-type → fraction decoder.

3. **Flexible CLI arguments** so that any combination of pixel inputs and patch inputs can be launched from the command line, enabling a clean ablation matrix across nodes.

---

## Science background (why this matters)

In 2A experiments, adding THOR alongside TerraMind at the bottleneck gave no gain or slight regression. At the time we concluded THOR was redundant. However the 7A finding changes this interpretation: TESSERA also looked harmful in 6A (IoU_B 0.168 → 0.017) when naively concatenated, but became beneficial in 7A once it got its own encoder with per-modality BatchNorm.

The mechanism: foundation model embeddings from different models have mismatched value ranges, channel covariance structure, and effective rank. A bare linear projection forces one matrix to simultaneously rescale two misaligned embedding spaces — the dominant modality hijacks the projection. Independent LayerNorm + 2-layer MLP per modality calibrates each space before fusion.

THOR and TerraMind are both S1/S2 foundation models but trained with different SSL objectives (TerraMind: MAE-style; THOR: different self-supervised task). Their embedding spaces are not aligned. The enhanced `PatchTokenStem` with per-modality LayerNorm is the right way to bring them into a common cross-attention space.

**Expected gain**: +0.005–0.015 if THOR was previously suppressed by TerraMind's larger embedding norm. Run as ablation after `7A_vegboost` baseline is confirmed.

