### Change 3 — Flexible CLI arguments

This is the most important change for enabling the ablation matrix. Make every modality optional via `--pixel-inputs` and `--patch-inputs`, and add new training-side flags.

#### 3a. `--pixel-inputs` (already exists, verify it works)
Comma-separated list of pixel-level embeddings. Accepted values: `alpha_earth`, `tessera`.
Examples:
```
--pixel-inputs alpha_earth
--pixel-inputs alpha_earth,tessera
```

The model must handle both cases:
- `alpha_earth` only → α-encoder only, τ-encoder disabled, height decoder uses α-encoder features only
- `alpha_earth,tessera` → full dual-encoder as designed

If `tessera` is absent, the height decoder cross-encoder bridge (α-bottleneck side input) still applies but the τ-encoder path is skipped entirely. The model degrades gracefully to a single-encoder variant.

#### 3b. `--patch-inputs` (already exists, extend it)
Comma-separated list of patch-level embeddings. Accepted values: `terramind_s1`, `terramind_s2`, `thor_s1`, `thor_s2`.
Examples:
```
--patch-inputs terramind_s1,terramind_s2
--patch-inputs terramind_s1,terramind_s2,thor_s1,thor_s2
--patch-inputs terramind_s2,thor_s2
--patch-inputs terramind_s1
```

Routing rules:
- Any `*_s1` token → height decoder injection
- Any `*_s2` token → fraction decoder injection
- Multiple tokens of the same sensor type → concatenated along token dimension before cross-attention
- If no `*_s1` tokens → height decoder receives no patch injection (relies on τ-encoder features only)
- If no `*_s2` tokens → fraction decoder receives no patch injection

The model must handle any subset gracefully without code changes — the routing is data-driven by the suffix of each embedding name.

