When all four runs finish, produce a comparison table:

```
| Experiment       | Proxy | IoU_B | IoU_V | IoU_W | RMSE_B | RMSE_V | Notes |
```

Then answer three questions:

1. **Does vegboost fix RMSE_V?** Compare n1 (`7A_vegboost`) RMSE_V to `7A_geocv_baseline` (3.996m on val). Target: ≤ 3.8m to safely clear the 3.9m cliff on the test set.

2. **Does THOR add value with enhanced stems?** Compare n2 (`7A_vegboost_thor`) to n1 (`7A_vegboost`). If proxy improves by more than 0.005, THOR is additive.

3. **Does the enhanced stem matter?** Compare n2 (`7A_vegboost_thor`, v2 stem) to n4 (`7A_vegboost_nostem`, v1 stem). If n2 > n4, the LayerNorm + 2-layer MLP is doing real work.

